.TH ZERODDS-XRCE-AGENTD.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-xrce-agentd.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-xrce-agentd(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/xrce-agentd.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the DDS-XRCE agent daemon listens for Micro
Clients and maps their sessions onto DDS. This config schema is a ZeroDDS
extension \(em DDS-XRCE 1.0 does not define an on-disk agent configuration
format. The parser that reads it is
.IR crates/xrce-agent/src/daemon/config.rs::DaemonConfig::from_config .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR log_level ", " vendor_id ", " session_timeout_secs ", "
.BR limits ", " discovery ", " listeners ", " type_files ", "
.BR xml_profile_files " and " qos_library_files .
.PP
An unknown top-level key, or an unknown key inside a known section, stops
the daemon from starting; the error names the file and line.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.TP
.B vendor_id
This agent's
.I XrceVendorId
as
.IR "\(dqmajor.minor\(dq" ,
each 0\(en255, e.g.
.I \(dq1.15\(dq
for eProsima's own registered agent id. Default
.I \(dq0.0\(dq
(none).
.TP
.B session_timeout_secs
Seconds of client inactivity \(em no message received on any stream \(em
before the session and every object it created are dropped. Default
.IR 60 .
.SS limits
.TP
.B max_clients
Maximum concurrent client sessions. Default
.IR 1024 .
.TP
.B max_objects_per_client
Maximum DDS-XRCE objects (participants, topics, publishers, subscribers,
writers, readers, types, QoS profiles) one client session may CREATE.
Default
.IR 256 .
.TP
.B max_pending_samples
Reliable-stream samples buffered per client while waiting on ACKNACK.
Default
.IR 256 .
.SS discovery
Multicast
.B GET_INFO
responder (DDS-XRCE 1.0 \(sc11.2.4): a Micro Client without a hardcoded
agent address finds this daemon here.
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B port
UDP port of the discovery multicast group. Default
.I 7400
(XRCE_DISCOVERY_PORT).
.SS listeners (list)
At least one entry is required; the default (when the key is entirely
absent) is a single
.I udp
listener on
.IR 0.0.0.0:2018 ,
eProsima's own default agent port. An entry is either a map with
.B kind
and the keys below, or one string
.IR udp:host:port ,
.I tcp:host:port
or
.I serial:device
(115200 baud) \(em the form
.B \-\-listen
writes.
.TP
.B kind
.IR udp " | " tcp " | " serial .
.TP
.B bind
.IR "host:port" .
Used by
.IR udp " and " tcp .
Default
.I 0.0.0.0:2018
for either.
.I tcp
frames messages with the DDS-XRCE \(sc11.3 2-byte length prefix.
.TP
.B device
Serial device path, e.g.
.IR /dev/ttyUSB0 .
Required for
.IR kind: \ serial ,
which needs the daemon's
.I serial
build feature and frames messages per DDS-XRCE Annex C. The packaged
systemd unit's
.B PrivateDevices
hardening blocks the device node; a serial deployment must override the
unit.
.TP
.B baud_rate
Integer baud rate for
.IR kind: \ serial .
Default
.IR 115200 .
.SS type_files (list)
Precompiled
.I TypeObject
values (XCDR2, as
.I TypeObject::to_bytes_le
produces \(em
.BR zerodds-idlc " or " zerodds-wire-probe
build one ahead of time), COMPLETE, one per file. A topic whose type name
matches an entry is created with that type for every client: key hashes,
dispose/unregister and the type announced to DDS peers. A client's own
OBJK_TYPE of the same name takes precedence for that client. The daemon
does not start if a file does not load, is not COMPLETE, or describes a
type other than its
.BR name .
Clients that send no type (the eProsima Micro-XRCE-DDS examples) need an
entry for keyed topics; without one a topic is forwarded opaque and
unkeyed.
.TP
.B name
The DDS type name this
.I TypeObject
is registered under.
.TP
.B file
Path to the binary
.IR TypeObject .
.SS xml_profile_files (list of strings)
Fast DDS profile files, the form the eProsima Micro-XRCE-DDS Agent reads
with
.BR -r :
a
.I <profiles>
root, or
.I <dds>
around
.IR <profiles> ", " <types> " and " <qos_library> .
A
.I REPRESENTATION_BY_REFERENCE
CREATE names the
.I profile_name
of a
.IR <participant> ", " <topic> ", " <publisher> ", " <subscriber> ", "
.IR <data_writer> " or " <data_reader>
there, which is read like the same element sent inline. A reference to a
profile no file defines is refused with
.IR STATUS_ERR_UNKNOWN_REFERENCE .
.I <types>
define topic types for every client, like
.BR type_files .
Other elements (
.IR <requester> ,
.IR <transport_descriptors> ,
\&...) are named on stderr at start and not used. The daemon does not
start if a file does not parse, defines a
.I profile_name
twice for one element, or a type twice.
.SS qos_library_files (list of strings)
DDS-XML 1.0
.I <qos_library>
documents. An attribute-form representation's
.I qos_profile=\(dqLibrary::Profile\(dq
names one of their profiles, resolved with its
.I base_name
chain; its DataWriter or DataReader QoS (and the Publisher or Subscriber
QoS for PARTITION and GROUP_DATA) apply before the representation's own
attributes. Policies the agent does not apply are named in the log.
.SH RELOAD
SIGHUP to
.BR zerodds-xrce-agentd (1)
re-reads this file (and its
.I xrce-agentd.d/
drop-ins) and applies
.BR log_level ", " limits.* ", " session_timeout_secs " and "
.BR discovery.enabled
without a restart. A changed
.BR listeners: ", " type_files: " or " xml_profile_files:
is logged and ignored until the daemon is restarted.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/xrce-agentd.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-xrce-agentd (1),
DDS-XRCE 1.0 (OMG formal/2023-03-01), DDS-XML.
